    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39054" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-sŏcer</span></b> ,
			ĕri, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a wife's grandfather</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cuique senex Nereus prosocer esse velit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					3, 74</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uxor, et nurus, et pronurus, viro, et socero,
					et prosocero furtum facere possunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					25, 2, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">erum cum prosocero meo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 5, 14</span></i>
			 (15), 8.</div>
